  "market_context": "Uptrend on US30 with price approaching 35,500–35,700 zone; RSI showed loss of momentum after two higher highs in price but lower high in RSI, occurring within the 70/30 RSI range.",
  "key_observation": "Price made a higher high near 35,547 while RSI formed a lower high, signaling bearish divergence and loss of upward momentum—confirmed when price failed to exceed the prior high.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified two consecutive price highs (around 35,528 and 35,547) on the 15-minute chart, both marked with red circles and downward arrows.",
    "Step 2: Compared those price highs to the corresponding RSI values and observed that while price made a higher high, RSI made a lower high—indicating bearish divergence and loss of momentum.",
    "Step 3: Noted that price was trading within the 70/30 RSI range at the time of divergence, satisfying the entry filter for the strategy.",
    "Step 4: Switched chart to Heikin Ashi candles to refine entry timing and looked specifically for a bearish candle with no upper wick.",
    "Step 5: Took short entry on the first Heikin Ashi bearish no-wick candle that rejected from the divergence zone, placing stop loss above the recent swing high.",
    "Step 6: Targeted a 1:2.4 risk-to-reward ratio, with take-profit achieved before the first bullish Heikin Ashi candle appeared."
  ],
  "outcome": "Trade achieved 1:2.4 risk-to-reward ratio; exited before first bullish Heikin Ashi candle.",
  "lessons": "Bearish RSI divergence within the 70/30 range is a high-probability reversal signal; confirming with Heikin Ashi no-wick candles improves entry precision and avoids false breakouts.",
